      "side": 1,
      "message": "This conflicts with the ACK contribution document here [1], which states that not-yet-upstreamed patches can be submitted to android-mainline:\n\n\u003e Submit patches to LKML first for an upstream review. If the patch is: [...] Not accepted upstream, submit it to android-mainline with a reference to the upstream submission or an explanation for why it wasn\u0027t submitted to LKML.\n\n\nThis patch fits the FROMLIST criteria at [2]:\n\n\u003e If the patch has been submitted to LKML, but not accepted into any maintainer tree\n\u003e tag the patch subject with FROMLIST:\n\n\nAnd I see the following FROMLIST patches were accepted into android-mainline [3].\n\nCould the guidance at [1] be corrected if FROMLIST patches are not allowed on android-mainline.\n\n---\n\n[1] https://source.android.com/docs/core/architecture/kernel/kernel-code#:~:text\u003dNot%20accepted%20upstream%2C%20submit%20it%20to%20android%2Dmainline%20with%20a%20reference%20to%20the%20upstream%20submission\n\n[2] https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android-mainline/README.md#:~:text\u003dIf%20the%20patch%20has%20been%20submitted%20to%20LKML%2C%20but%20not%20accepted%20into%20any%20maintainer%20tree\n\n[3] https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/q/project:kernel/common+branch:android-mainline+subject:%22FROMLIST:%22+status:merged",
